    "name": "Takahara to Chikatsuyu-oji",
    "theme": "Immersion",
    "narrative": "This is the day that defines the Kumano Kodo. The forest is everything. Cedar and cypress close overhead, moss covers every surface, and the ancient cobblestone paths — some laid centuries ago by monks — guide your feet through terrain that feels older than history. At Tsugizakura-oji, 800-year-old cedar trees tower above a tiny wooden shrine. The Oji were subsidiary shrines where pilgrims paused to make offerings and purify themselves. Now they are portals.",
    "closing": "When did the forest stop being scenery and become presence?",
